  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A metal cube X of length L is heated gaining thermal energy Q. Its temperature rises by ΔT. A second cube Y, of length 2L, made of the same material, gains thermal energy of 2Q.</p>\n<p>What is the temperature rise of Y?</p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{Δ T}{8}\"></span></li><li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{Δ T}{4}\"></span></li><li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Δ T\"></span></li><li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2 Δ T\"></span></li></ol>"
